# UI overlap check (required)

After finishing any UI / layout / chrome change:

1. Mentally map every fixed/absolute control on the viewport (Menu, language, theme, dock, FABs, page actions, map controls, sheets).
2. Ensure no two tappable controls share the same corner or collide at common breakpoints (desktop ~1120px and mobile ~390px).
3. Prefer consolidating page actions into one panel/cluster; leave site chrome (Menu, language, dock) in reserved safe zones.
4. If you moved or added overlays (full-bleed maps, drawers, sheets), re-check z-index and hit targets so floating page UI does not cover Menu / language / dock.
5. Do not consider the task done until overlaps are fixed or explicitly called out to the user.
